# Text is stored AND checked out as LF on every platform. This machine has
# core.autocrlf=true, which would otherwise rewrite the seed documents (CLAUDE.md,
# CONTEXT.md, plan.md are LF today) with CRLF on the next checkout -- files CLAUDE.md
# forbids touching should not be mutated by a git default.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Frozen golden fixtures are DATA, not text: their exact bytes are the test input
# (CONTEXT §8 F7/F10; CLAUDE.md rule 3). `-text` disables all line-ending translation, so
# the checked-out bytes are exactly the committed bytes -- these CSVs are CRLF as produced
# by the PoC run and must stay that way. Listed last: later rules win in .gitattributes.
poc/data/** -text
tests/fixtures/** -text
